WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.110 --> 00:00:05.710
Stranger Things is this cool new sorta mystery-scifi-horror-drama
type deal from Netflix.

00:00:05.710 --> 00:00:10.289
It’s set in the 80s, and it borrows a lot
from the films of that time, like E.T., and

00:00:10.289 --> 00:00:11.289
Alien.

00:00:11.289 --> 00:00:15.240
The story begins with the disappearance of
a boy called Will from the town of Hawkins,

00:00:15.240 --> 00:00:19.040
Indiana, and the mystery quickly deepens with
the appearance of a girl with psychic powers,

00:00:19.040 --> 00:00:22.970
a shadowy government agency, and a monster
from another dimension.

00:00:22.970 --> 00:00:27.420
By the end of the season Will is found but
there are still heaps of unresolved questions

00:00:27.420 --> 00:00:29.910
– like what’s up with Hopper and the g-men?

00:00:29.910 --> 00:00:32.390
What is the monster, and how does the Upside
Down work?

00:00:32.390 --> 00:00:33.390
What happened to Eleven?

00:00:33.390 --> 00:00:37.510
And why did Nancy hook up with the douchebag
Steve instead of the sensitive Jonathan?

00:00:37.510 --> 00:00:38.739
Was it the hair?

00:00:38.739 --> 00:00:40.090
It was probably the hair.

00:00:40.090 --> 00:00:44.890
But still let’s have a look at what happened
in Stranger Things Season 1, beginning at

00:00:44.890 --> 00:00:47.030
the very beginning.

00:00:47.030 --> 00:00:52.520
In the fifties and sixties, the CIA conducted
secret experiments in a program called MKUltra,

00:00:52.520 --> 00:00:57.399
using drugs like LSD to investigate mind control,
brainwashing and interrogation techniques

00:00:57.399 --> 00:01:01.450
– which is a real thing that happened, by
the way – but in Stranger Things, some of

00:01:01.450 --> 00:01:06.220
these experiments take place at the Hawkins
National Laboratory, led by a certain Dr.

00:01:06.220 --> 00:01:07.220
Brenner.

00:01:07.220 --> 00:01:10.720
And one of Brenner’s subjects back in the
day was a woman called Terry Ives.

00:01:10.720 --> 00:01:15.240
We learn that Terry was pregnant while she
was being experimented on with drugs, so naturally,

00:01:15.240 --> 00:01:19.130
her child was born with psychic powers – like
telekinesis.

00:01:19.130 --> 00:01:23.550
Terry named the child Jane, but Jane was taken
away from her by Brenner, who covered up the

00:01:23.550 --> 00:01:26.729
kidnapping saying Terry actually had a miscarriage.

00:01:26.729 --> 00:01:30.479
Terry tried to sue Brenner to get her daughter
back, but these attempts failed, and Terry

00:01:30.479 --> 00:01:33.820
seems to have declined into a drugged-out
stupor.

00:01:33.820 --> 00:01:39.229
Meanwhile Jane grew up in the Hawkins lab,
where she was tattooed with her new name – Eleven.

00:01:39.229 --> 00:01:43.330
Eleven calls Dr Brenner “papa”, which
might mean Dr. Brenner lied and told El that

00:01:43.330 --> 00:01:48.159
he was her dad, or maybe he really is her
dad, maybe he had some relationship with Terry,

00:01:48.159 --> 00:01:49.409
we don’t know.

00:01:49.409 --> 00:01:52.280
But in any case El is treated cruelly at the
Lab.

00:01:52.280 --> 00:01:56.210
Brenner subjects her to lots of experiments
– making her break things with her mind,

00:01:56.210 --> 00:01:58.160
and perceive things from a distance.

00:01:58.160 --> 00:02:02.259
Sometimes he put Eleven in a sensory deprivation
tank, where Eleven’s able to psychically

00:02:02.259 --> 00:02:06.569
project herself into a weird dark void where
she can interact with people who are far away

00:02:06.569 --> 00:02:11.989
– this is during the Cold War, so Brenner
and his CIA buddies use her to spy on Russians.

00:02:11.989 --> 00:02:15.840
But also in this darkness Eleven encounters
a monster.

00:02:15.840 --> 00:02:20.370
The monster presumably isn’t physically
in this dark space, but is in its own dimension,

00:02:20.370 --> 00:02:24.830
the Upside Down, just as the Russian is in
Russia, and Eleven’s in the tank, but by

00:02:24.830 --> 00:02:30.040
projecting herself through this dark space,
Eleven is able to reach across the dimensions,

00:02:30.040 --> 00:02:34.379
and under the orders of Brenner, she makes
contact with the monster, somehow causing

00:02:34.379 --> 00:02:40.090
“a tear in time and space”, making a gate,
a portal into the monster’s dimension, allowing

00:02:40.090 --> 00:02:42.480
it to emerge into Hawkins.

00:02:42.480 --> 00:02:46.459
In the commotion, Eleven escapes the Lab by
crawling through a drain pipe, meanwhile the

00:02:46.459 --> 00:02:51.660
monster starts to hunt animals and people
in Hawkins – at the start of Episode 1,

00:02:51.660 --> 00:02:53.110
it takes Will.

00:02:53.110 --> 00:02:56.819
So this kicks off the human drama of the story
– we see Will’s mother Joyce frantically

00:02:56.819 --> 00:03:00.910
trying to connect with her son, and Will’s
older brother Jonathan searching, in his angst

00:03:00.910 --> 00:03:02.120
and alienation.

00:03:02.120 --> 00:03:05.480
We see the cop Jim Hopper, still haunted by
his daughter’s death.

00:03:05.480 --> 00:03:09.269
And when Eleven escapes from the Lab she groups
up with Will’s friends Mike and Lucas and

00:03:09.269 --> 00:03:14.130
Dustin, who teach her loyalty and normalcy
and love, there’s also Mike’s sister Nancy,

00:03:14.130 --> 00:03:18.099
who’s growing up, trying to work out who
she is, discovering sex – like, when we

00:03:18.099 --> 00:03:22.900
first see Nancy, Dustin offers her some sausage
and pepperoni pizza, which Nancy declines,

00:03:22.900 --> 00:03:27.269
and this refusal to ‘take the sausage’
kinda foreshadows her conflict over whether

00:03:27.269 --> 00:03:31.250
to sleep with her boyfriend Steve, or to listen
to her friend Barb and stay a virgin.

00:03:31.250 --> 00:03:35.870
Barb, for her part, dies and no one seems
to care, but Steve gets a redemption of sorts,

00:03:35.870 --> 00:03:37.959
after being an asshole early on.

00:03:37.959 --> 00:03:41.130
In the end, Nancy and Steve are together,
but there’s still a bit of a love triangle

00:03:41.130 --> 00:03:42.360
with Jonathan.

00:03:42.360 --> 00:03:46.110
So yeah, there’s some interesting drama
happening, but the really juicy mysteries

00:03:46.110 --> 00:03:48.670
surround the Upside Down.

00:03:48.670 --> 00:03:51.650
The Upside Down seems to be a sort of “alternate
dimension”.

00:03:51.650 --> 00:03:55.260
It has the same stuff in in it as the real
world – all the buildings and trees and

00:03:55.260 --> 00:04:01.220
cars of Hawkins are there – but everything’s
dark and dead and decayed, cold and empty.

00:04:01.220 --> 00:04:05.709
When stuff moves or changes in the real Hawkins,
nothing seems to change or move in the Upside

00:04:05.709 --> 00:04:11.459
Down, so it’s almost like this is a snapshot,
a frozen moment in time, perhaps of what Hawkins

00:04:11.459 --> 00:04:16.539
was like at the moment of contact, when Eleven
touched the monster – maybe it was at that

00:04:16.539 --> 00:04:19.949
moment that this whole dimension was created.

00:04:19.949 --> 00:04:24.849
Or maybe the Upside Down used to be alive
and normal like Hawkins, but it was infected

00:04:24.849 --> 00:04:28.229
by this weird toxic growth we see in the Upside
Down.

00:04:28.229 --> 00:04:33.229
There are vines or tentacles on the ground,
slime on the walls, particles in the air,

00:04:33.229 --> 00:04:38.539
the gate seems to grow, and wherever the monster
goes, slime spreads.

00:04:38.539 --> 00:04:42.759
Maybe this is like an interdimensional disease,
spreading from parallel world to parallel

00:04:42.759 --> 00:04:45.219
world, infecting the multiverse.

00:04:45.219 --> 00:04:47.110
Or maybe this is a time travel thing.

00:04:47.110 --> 00:04:52.169
Maybe the Upside Down is the future of Hawkins,
it’s what it’ll become after being infected

00:04:52.169 --> 00:04:54.750
– by its own future.

00:04:54.750 --> 00:04:58.969
This is all wild speculation, but whatever
the Upside Down is, it’s clearly closely

00:04:58.969 --> 00:05:04.030
connected to Hawkins – the dimensions affect
each other in lots of different ways.

00:05:04.030 --> 00:05:08.419
Activity in the Upside Down can cause electrical
disturbance in Hawkins, Will and Joyce can

00:05:08.419 --> 00:05:13.009
even use lights to communicate, though we
don’t how this works on Will’s end – how

00:05:13.009 --> 00:05:16.749
can he even see the lights and letters from
the Upside Down?

00:05:16.749 --> 00:05:20.689
Some people think this means Will has psychic
powers like Eleven – which could maybe also

00:05:20.689 --> 00:05:26.009
explain this weird gate-like thing Will seems
to open – but the evidence still isn’t

00:05:26.009 --> 00:05:27.009
strong.

00:05:27.009 --> 00:05:30.589
Anyway the Upside Down can also affect Hawkins
through magnetism – apparently the gate

00:05:30.589 --> 00:05:32.919
has a strong electromagnetic field.

00:05:32.919 --> 00:05:37.210
And sound can cross the dimensions – Jonno
hears Nancy when she’s in the Upside Down.

00:05:37.210 --> 00:05:42.259
The very walls in Hawkins can give way to
the Upside Down – which allows the monster

00:05:42.259 --> 00:05:43.259
to enter.

00:05:43.259 --> 00:05:48.500
The monster, also called the Demogorgon, is
a creature that looks kinda like a human,

00:05:48.500 --> 00:05:54.279
but with long arms, and five unfolding ‘petals’
of teeth instead of a face.

00:05:54.279 --> 00:05:58.449
After Eleven makes the gate, the monster is
able to make small portals of its own, crossing

00:05:58.449 --> 00:06:02.289
into Hawkins, to drag prey into the Upside
Down.

00:06:02.289 --> 00:06:05.210
Like a shark, it’s apparently drawn by blood.

00:06:05.210 --> 00:06:10.461
The monster hunts for food, but it also uses
prey for other purposes – in Episode 8,

00:06:10.461 --> 00:06:16.009
we see that Will has been stuck in some gross
organic fleshy web, like in Alien, with a

00:06:16.009 --> 00:06:18.580
slimy tentacle down his throat like a Facehugger.

00:06:18.580 --> 00:06:23.439
Maybe, like in Alien, the creature uses human
hosts to reproduce.

00:06:23.439 --> 00:06:28.009
Maybe the little slugs that emerge from the
bodies of Barb and Will are little baby demogorgons.

00:06:28.009 --> 00:06:33.020
Though that doesn’t explain the hatched
egg we see earlier on in the Upside Down – maybe

00:06:33.020 --> 00:06:37.199
that’s the egg the monster hatched from,
but if so, what laid the egg?

00:06:37.199 --> 00:06:39.069
It looks too big to come out of a Demogorgon.

00:06:39.069 --> 00:06:44.219
Also, the first time we see the monster, it
looks like its eating that same egg.

00:06:44.219 --> 00:06:48.789
So between the monster, the eggs, the facehugger-tentacles,
and the cough-up slugs, there must be some

00:06:48.789 --> 00:06:53.610
complex symbiotic life-cycle happening here,
there must be more creatures involved – maybe

00:06:53.610 --> 00:06:58.509
there are big egg-laying slug queens, or juvenile
demogorgons out there.

00:06:58.509 --> 00:07:01.309
Maybe this creature is an alien.

00:07:01.309 --> 00:07:04.970
Or maybe the monster is something more human.

00:07:04.970 --> 00:07:09.620
One popular theory is that the monster somehow
represents Eleven’s darker half, like, maybe

00:07:09.620 --> 00:07:14.409
the monster is a psychic manifestation of
her anger and fear, and her suffering at the

00:07:14.409 --> 00:07:19.860
Hawkins Lab, and that in that moment of contact
when the gate was made, she brought the monster

00:07:19.860 --> 00:07:24.099
out of her subconscious and into the real
world – maybe that’s what El means when

00:07:24.099 --> 00:07:26.319
she says “I’m the monster”.

00:07:26.319 --> 00:07:30.699
This idea could help explain some similarities
between El and the monster, like in Episode

00:07:30.699 --> 00:07:35.580
1, we see the monster open a lock without
touching it, just as Eleven locks a lock – the

00:07:35.580 --> 00:07:39.399
monster appears to have telekinetic abilities,
just like El.

00:07:39.399 --> 00:07:44.240
Also, Eleven seems to recognise a photo of
Will without having met him before – maybe

00:07:44.240 --> 00:07:49.360
she recognises him because her other half,
the monster, has abducted Will.

00:07:49.360 --> 00:07:53.499
When El defeats the monster, both she and
the monster disappear, as though they kinda

00:07:53.499 --> 00:07:55.279
cancelled each other out.

00:07:55.279 --> 00:07:59.849
Maybe El and the monster merged back into
one, the monster returning to its place in

00:07:59.849 --> 00:08:03.429
El’s consciousness – maybe changing her
for the worse.

00:08:03.429 --> 00:08:07.989
All that said, if El is the monster, how do
we explain the complex biology of the Upside

00:08:07.989 --> 00:08:08.989
Down?

00:08:08.989 --> 00:08:11.439
Could that have possibly come from El’s
mind?

00:08:11.439 --> 00:08:15.729
Finally, it’s very interesting that when
El uses her powers, we see the same weird

00:08:15.729 --> 00:08:20.080
electrical effects that are associated with
the Upside Down, so there’s gotta be some

00:08:20.080 --> 00:08:21.080
link here.

00:08:21.080 --> 00:08:25.439
It’s all very uncertain, but there are clearly
strong connections between Eleven and the

00:08:25.439 --> 00:08:28.729
monster and the Upside Down.

00:08:28.729 --> 00:08:33.320
At the end of Season 1, El and the monster
disappear, Will comes home, and we get a ‘one

00:08:33.320 --> 00:08:36.349
month later’, where everything seems calm
and normal.

00:08:36.349 --> 00:08:40.579
The Byers have Christmas dinner, the boys
play D and D. Steve and Nancy get Jon a camera

00:08:40.579 --> 00:08:42.539
to replace the one Steve broke.

00:08:42.539 --> 00:08:43.550
All seems well.

00:08:43.550 --> 00:08:48.060
But we see some newspaper clippings that show
there’s still a lot going on.

00:08:48.060 --> 00:08:52.540
Joyce has told the media about Brenner’s
experiments at the Lab, leading to a “massive

00:08:52.540 --> 00:08:53.540
investigation”.

00:08:53.540 --> 00:08:56.910
The coroner who was involved in Will’s fake
body has been caught, and there’s a shake-up

00:08:56.910 --> 00:09:00.459
among the State Troopers, who worked with
Brenner’s people to cover stuff up.

00:09:00.459 --> 00:09:05.170
It seems that the secrets of the Hawkins Lab
are being revealed to the world – but it

00:09:05.170 --> 00:09:09.829
may be that nothing comes of this, because
MKUltra was supposedly exposed before.

00:09:09.829 --> 00:09:11.310
But there are more cool details.

00:09:11.310 --> 00:09:16.170
The article quotes someone called Ives expressing
disgust about the Lab, which is weird cause

00:09:16.170 --> 00:09:20.400
Becky Ives doesn’t seem to believe any of
this conspiracy stuff, and Terry Ives doesn’t

00:09:20.400 --> 00:09:22.540
seem to speakj – so what’s going on?

00:09:22.540 --> 00:09:24.100
Is Terry talking again?

00:09:24.100 --> 00:09:27.240
Could she maybe have a reunion with her daughter,
Eleven?

00:09:27.240 --> 00:09:29.889
Finally, the article mentions Brenner.

00:09:29.889 --> 00:09:35.000
Last we saw him, he was attacked by the monster
– but this suggests he survives, and comments

00:09:35.000 --> 00:09:39.290
from Brenner’s actor and the Duffer Brothers
have all but confirmed that we will be seeing

00:09:39.290 --> 00:09:40.629
him again.

00:09:40.629 --> 00:09:42.980
Which brings us to Season 2.

00:09:42.980 --> 00:09:47.230
Season 2 of Stranger Things is set for release
in 2017, and there’s already a lot of info

00:09:47.230 --> 00:09:48.519
out about it.

00:09:48.519 --> 00:09:51.490
The show’s creators, the Duffer Brothers,
have said the season will be like a “sequel”

00:09:51.490 --> 00:09:52.649
to the first.

00:09:52.649 --> 00:09:55.930
Apparently it’ll explore the repercussions
of everything that happened last season, while

00:09:55.930 --> 00:09:58.540
also introducing “new problems and questions”.

00:09:58.540 --> 00:10:03.019
There’ll be new characters, including Max
and Billy and Roman.

00:10:03.019 --> 00:10:07.889
Max is a sort of a tomboy with a complicated
history, Billy is her step-brother, hyper-confident

00:10:07.889 --> 00:10:12.459
and violent, and Roman is an outsider with
a rough past who seeks revenge for a great

00:10:12.459 --> 00:10:14.899
loss suffered at an early age.

00:10:14.899 --> 00:10:18.399
All these guys sound potentially interesting,
it’ll be cool to see how they fit with the

00:10:18.399 --> 00:10:19.560
existing cast.

00:10:19.560 --> 00:10:24.560
Also, a teaser trailer for Season 2 has released
nine episode titles, which give tantalising

00:10:24.560 --> 00:10:26.300
hints of what’s to come.

00:10:26.300 --> 00:10:31.270
The first title, Madmax is evocative of the
Mad Max movies, but probably refers to the

00:10:31.270 --> 00:10:32.270
character Max.

00:10:32.270 --> 00:10:36.360
The Boy Who Came Back to Life has a Harry
Potter vibe, but we know this refers to Will,

00:10:36.360 --> 00:10:37.420
just like on the newspaper.

00:10:37.420 --> 00:10:41.800
A lot of the other stuff could kinda mean
anything – the pumpkin patch could maybe

00:10:41.800 --> 00:10:47.170
be like a field of eggs like in Alien, the
palace could be some kind of important base,

00:10:47.170 --> 00:10:52.689
the storm could be general metaphorical conflict
or maybe, more literally, some kinda interdimensional

00:10:52.689 --> 00:10:54.529
Upside Down-y kinda storm?

00:10:54.529 --> 00:10:59.540
A pollywog is a tadpole, like the pokéman,
which could perhaps refer to these slugs if

00:10:59.540 --> 00:11:02.029
they’re, like, baby demogorgons.

00:11:02.029 --> 00:11:05.959
The secret cabin sounds like a good place
for Eleven or someone to hide.

00:11:05.959 --> 00:11:11.139
And the brain could maybe refer to some intelligence
behind the creatures of the Upside Down, maybe

00:11:11.139 --> 00:11:13.430
some hivemind shit.

00:11:13.430 --> 00:11:17.519
Finally the lost brother might refer to a
test subject like Eleven who was taken away

00:11:17.519 --> 00:11:21.910
from their sibling – maybe this is the “great
loss” Roman suffered.

00:11:21.910 --> 00:11:25.560
So there are a million cool new possibilities
for Season 2 here, but let’s also have a

00:11:25.560 --> 00:11:29.940
look at what might happen to the characters
we already and love.

00:11:29.940 --> 00:11:33.779
Season 1 ends with this creepy scene where
Will coughs up a slug, just like the one that

00:11:33.779 --> 00:11:39.000
came out of Barb, and then then seems to flicker
for a moment into the Upside Down.

00:11:39.000 --> 00:11:42.970
Apparently the Upside Down has done something
bad to Will, and there are a lots of different

00:11:42.970 --> 00:11:45.209
theories about what this may be.

00:11:45.209 --> 00:11:49.459
Since he got facehugger-tentacled, some people
think he’s got monster eggs or monster slugs

00:11:49.459 --> 00:11:54.350
growing inside him, or even that he’s turning
into a monster.

00:11:54.350 --> 00:11:58.189
Another possibility is that his time in the
Upside Down has given him some kind of power

00:11:58.189 --> 00:12:01.839
to see into that dimension, that he’s connected
somehow.

00:12:01.839 --> 00:12:04.870
But there also questions about how this has
affected Will as a person.

00:12:04.870 --> 00:12:07.290
Like, he’s seen some shit, right?

00:12:07.290 --> 00:12:12.439
He struggled to survive in a nightmare bizarro
world, hunted a horrific monster, isolated

00:12:12.439 --> 00:12:17.319
from all he knows, for a week, at the age
of, like twelve – that must have had an

00:12:17.319 --> 00:12:21.370
impact on him, surely, so Season 2 might explore
this.

00:12:21.370 --> 00:12:24.889
But the character we really care about here
is Eleven, right?

00:12:24.889 --> 00:12:26.999
When and how will she come back?

00:12:26.999 --> 00:12:30.880
We do know that she’ll be back if only cause
of those waffles Hopper leaves out for her.

00:12:30.880 --> 00:12:32.880
But what’ll happen with her character?

00:12:32.880 --> 00:12:36.769
She’s got this great identity conflict,
where one hand she wants to be pretty, and

00:12:36.769 --> 00:12:40.529
she wants to be normal, while on the other
hand, she grew up as a government “weapon”,

00:12:40.529 --> 00:12:42.550
and sees herself as a monster.

00:12:42.550 --> 00:12:46.209
This is why her relationship with Mike is
so beautiful – he doesn’t want her to

00:12:46.209 --> 00:12:49.759
wear a wig, or be a weapon – he accepts
her for who she is.

00:12:49.759 --> 00:12:54.381
But El still has a long way to go in working
out her identity, and hopefully Season 2 will

00:12:54.381 --> 00:12:56.290
continue to explore this.

00:12:56.290 --> 00:12:58.040
There are also questions about her powers.

00:12:58.040 --> 00:13:02.100
We’ve seen El throw a van into the air,
levitate people, smoosh peoples brains, make

00:13:02.100 --> 00:13:03.290
a kid pee.

00:13:03.290 --> 00:13:07.320
Project herself across space and dimensions,
rip holes in spacetime itself.

00:13:07.320 --> 00:13:09.410
What else might she be capable of?

00:13:09.410 --> 00:13:13.209
We got a taste of her greater power in her
confrontation with the monster – her eyes

00:13:13.209 --> 00:13:16.839
go kinda red and she goes all Super Saiyan
on the monster’s ass.

00:13:16.839 --> 00:13:21.060
There are lots of parallels here with the
Marvel Comics character Jean Grey, who transforms

00:13:21.060 --> 00:13:24.660
into a massively powerful psychic being called
Dark Phoenix.

00:13:24.660 --> 00:13:29.639
The comic in which this happens, X-Men #134,
is specifically referenced in Stranger Things

00:13:29.639 --> 00:13:31.370
by Dustin and Will.

00:13:31.370 --> 00:13:36.339
So maybe, as with Jean Grey, we’ll see a
wilder, much more destructive side to Eleven

00:13:36.339 --> 00:13:38.350
in Season 2.

00:13:38.350 --> 00:13:40.410
Another great character is Hopper.

00:13:40.410 --> 00:13:44.480
Season 1 explored his grief over the death
of his daughter Sarah, and we see his memories

00:13:44.480 --> 00:13:47.120
of her driving him in the search for Will.

00:13:47.120 --> 00:13:50.170
It seems like he still needs some closure
here, and there are hints that there might

00:13:50.170 --> 00:13:56.420
be more to reveal about Sarah’s death – Hopper’s
actor describes it as a secret.

00:13:56.420 --> 00:13:59.629
Some fans speculate that Sarah might have
had powers like El.

00:13:59.629 --> 00:14:03.879
Also there are also questions about Hopper’s
connections to Brenner and the government

00:14:03.879 --> 00:14:04.879
men.

00:14:04.879 --> 00:14:08.060
In Episode 8 we see Hopper get in a black
government car – what’s he up to?

00:14:08.060 --> 00:14:12.440
We know earlier in the Episode Hop made a
deal with Doctor Brenner – Brenner let Hop

00:14:12.440 --> 00:14:17.439
and Joyce through the gate, and in return,
Hop gave Brenner… what?

00:14:17.439 --> 00:14:21.819
The likely answer is that Hop told Brenner
where to find Mike and El – that’s how

00:14:21.819 --> 00:14:24.129
Brenner knew to come to the high school gym.

00:14:24.129 --> 00:14:28.559
You can argue that that was the right strategic
move – Will’s life was at stake, and Eleven

00:14:28.559 --> 00:14:32.430
can protect herself, but still – Hop totally
betrayed them.

00:14:32.430 --> 00:14:35.250
If Joyce and the boys find out, we could have
problems.

00:14:35.250 --> 00:14:39.920
Finally, it’d be great to find out more
Brenner and the Lab and the government men,

00:14:39.920 --> 00:14:43.661
the “bad men” – we don’t even know
what to call these guys cause we really don’t

00:14:43.661 --> 00:14:45.129
know who they are.

00:14:45.129 --> 00:14:50.079
Hop suggests “the CIA, the NSA, Department
of Energy”, others say they’re military,

00:14:50.079 --> 00:14:54.509
we know they were working with the State Troopers,
but it’s really unclear who these guys are.

00:14:54.509 --> 00:14:59.399
We’ve seen them do some extreme shit – they
murdered Benny and made it look like a suicide,

00:14:59.399 --> 00:15:03.410
they drugged and bugged Hop, they moved Barb’s
car to make it look like she ran away, they

00:15:03.410 --> 00:15:06.900
made a lifelike fake corpse of a dead child.

00:15:06.900 --> 00:15:10.700
They listen in on everyone’s phone calls,
they use these Hawkins Power and Light guys

00:15:10.700 --> 00:15:11.899
to spy.

00:15:11.899 --> 00:15:16.370
Whoever they are, these guys have heaps of
resources, and are ruthless in pursuing their

00:15:16.370 --> 00:15:17.370
goals.

00:15:17.370 --> 00:15:18.809
But what are their goals?

00:15:18.809 --> 00:15:21.970
Clearly they’re interested in Eleven’s
psychic powers, but there must be more to

00:15:21.970 --> 00:15:25.430
it – why was Brenner so keen to get El to
make contact with the monster?

00:15:25.430 --> 00:15:27.829
What do they know about the Upside Down?

00:15:27.829 --> 00:15:30.220
Who else might they have experimented on?

00:15:30.220 --> 00:15:35.220
If Eleven is the eleventh subject, are there
ten or more other subjects out there?

00:15:35.220 --> 00:15:39.279
The Duffers have promised “a lot more backstory”
bout Brenner and Eleven and all that, so it’ll

00:15:39.279 --> 00:15:42.430
be awesome to dig deeper into that history.

00:15:42.430 --> 00:15:47.180
So basically Season 1 of Stranger Things was
pretty bloody great, and the sequel Season

00:15:47.180 --> 00:15:48.810
2 is looking pretty good too.

00:15:48.810 --> 00:15:52.579
What questions would you like to see answered
next season and what do you want to see next

00:15:52.579 --> 00:15:53.970
from Alt Shift X?

00:15:53.970 --> 00:15:57.729
Remember to like and subscribe, and check
out our Game of Thrones vids if you’re keen.

